    "axes": "+Y up, metres"
  },
  "limits": "Only straight sides (no curved profile; see a lathe for that) and a constant-radius bore. Caps and walls own separate vertices for sharp shading, so closed results are watertight after welding. A cone apex holds one vertex per segment.",
